                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a09478a6-ce5e-3907-8bfb-07b162e56eb0",
                        "entry_id": "4d985560-4ee9-3774-b32d-c7df46a7f62a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. то же, что крапивная лихорадка; кожное заболевание преимущественно аллергического происхождения, характеризующееся быстрым появлением сильно зудящих, плоско приподнятых бледно-розовых волдырей, сходных по виду с волдырями от ожога крапивой"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f383f48-c1ce-49cd-be59-d6caebfae447",
                                "sense_id": "a09478a6-ce5e-3907-8bfb-07b162e56eb0",
                                "text": "Адреностимуляторы для парентерального введения — препараты для неотложной помощи при анафилактических реакциях и тяжелой острой крапивнице."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "612080da-061c-498a-a5b4-0759085884f6",
                        "source_entry_id": "4d985560-4ee9-3774-b32d-c7df46a7f62a",
                        "source_sense_id": "a09478a6-ce5e-3907-8bfb-07b162e56eb0",
                        "target_lang_word": "urticaria",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "urticaria",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "197a45ee-aaee-3e7a-bf62-48411477c7c9",
                                        "entry_id": "fe1bdea9-88a6-3879-b656-302606b479d2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Itchy, swollen, red areas of the skin which can appear quickly in response to an allergen or other conditions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b63e738-801c-40dc-bd85-47732eb89ab5",
                                                "sense_id": "197a45ee-aaee-3e7a-bf62-48411477c7c9",
                                                "text": "\"And the cramps when my body - like a badly articulated skeleton - would all get twisted into one rigid tangle! But now, except some dyspepsia and urticaria of the palms, I am free from pain.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32aa161e-85ee-4f50-9353-5911198f64e6",
                                                "sense_id": "197a45ee-aaee-3e7a-bf62-48411477c7c9",
                                                "text": "So when I was diagnosed with a fairly difficult-to-treat disease called idiopathic angioedema and chronic urticaria (a fancy way of saying we don’t know why you swell and hey, enjoy the 24/7 hives) six months ago, I wasn't quite sure how to cope."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "618cacf5-6a16-4e2e-9431-ceb95ec41b1d",
                        "source_entry_id": "4d985560-4ee9-3774-b32d-c7df46a7f62a",
                        "source_sense_id": "a09478a6-ce5e-3907-8bfb-07b162e56eb0",
                        "target_lang_word": "hives",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hives",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e5e17b2-202b-3589-ae2e-78e7a6f8292b",
                                        "entry_id": "bb503212-b446-3680-bc2e-4b951caf6b45",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Itchy, swollen, red areas of the skin which can appear quickly in response to an allergen or due to other conditions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural",
                                            "plural-normally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21ee858b-cfc1-402e-8639-bd11623e8b16",
                                                "sense_id": "9e5e17b2-202b-3589-ae2e-78e7a6f8292b",
                                                "text": "So when I was diagnosed with a fairly difficult-to-treat disease called idiopathic angioedema and chronic urticaria (a fancy way of saying we don’t know why you swell and hey, enjoy the 24/7 hives) six months ago, I wasn't quite sure how to cope."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76bae2bb-c009-41f7-af27-4a6266d898c2",
                                                "sense_id": "9e5e17b2-202b-3589-ae2e-78e7a6f8292b",
                                                "text": "When she recovers enough to look down at her arms [...] she blinks to see them covered in faint, but rising, puffy welts. Hives. She's breaking out in hives."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "hives",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39914de7-3d98-306a-8627-caef8ce22f12",
                                        "entry_id": "3ac447e9-4892-3981-8730-7572385ebcf5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "plural of hive"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "hives",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db2ce5ef-df59-3579-afba-bdfdda467d50",
                                        "entry_id": "f6020cca-0427-3900-bb9b-b6f481fdbfb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "third-person singular simple present indicative of hive"
                                        ],
